  "protocol": "Seven alternating fresh-Node sets; 24 pinned Kodak photographs. Kernel setup decodes outside timer; 25 warmup batches then 200 timed batches = 4800 calls. All variants consume output via base64/checksum. Rust includes validation, hash copy, owned RGBA output for decode or synchronous PNG base64. cachedJS reuses bounded cosine/coefficient scratch; cachedPNG adds fixed typed-array PNG/CRC/base64 control. Initialization is incremental after common static imports, not whole-process startup. Complete previews: first 24-image batch, one warmup batch, 72 timed sequential previews, no persistent preview cache. LQIP unchanged control. Props: 24 registered URL artifacts, 100 warmup batches then 10000 batches (240000 calls), empty provider map; canonical attribute digest must match. All output digests must match. Serial suites on uncontrolled desktop.",
